---
// src/pages/about.astro
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout title="about" description={`About ${SITE.author} and ${SITE.title}.`}>
  <article>
    <h1>about</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE.title} is the public lab notebook of <a href={SITE.portfolio}>{SITE.author}</a>,
      a developer and educator based in Antwerp. Projects in data science,
      AI, IoT, web platforms, and the occasional cultural side-project.
    </p>
    <h2>format</h2>
    <p>
      Posts use one of four formats: build-along, post-mortem, paper summary,
      or weeknote. Each project post follows an explicit method section
      (question · data · procedure · metric · result · limits).
    </p>
    <h2>buckets</h2>
    <p>The bucket column in the listing tags each post by category:</p>
    <table>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>A</strong></td><td>niche projects (mobility, inland shipping, e-bike, edge IoT, circular, cultural-public data)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>B</strong></td><td>reuse projects (existing artefacts as research field)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>C</strong></td><td>classical ML on messy real-world data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>D</strong></td><td>methodology and statistics projects</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>E</strong></td><td>writing and reading (paper summaries, proposals)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>F</strong></td><td>cultural, absurd, installation</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Built with Astro on Cloudflare Pages. Source on
      <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>. Code MIT, prose CC-BY-SA. Cookieless
      analytics via Cloudflare Web Analytics. Interactive Python demos run
      client-side in Pyodide; nothing is sent to a server.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
